layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | Notifications tell you when something needs you, so you do not have to keep the app open. Buildyboy can deliver
    | them in two ways: as
    strong Web Push
    | notifications to the browsers and phones where you switched them on, and optionally to an
    strong ntfy
    | topic. Everything is set up in
    strong Settings → Notifications
    | .

  h2#web-push Turning on Web Push on a device
  p Repeat this on every device that should receive notifications. Each device is switched on separately.
  ol
    li
      | On a phone, first install Buildyboy on the home screen (see
      a(href="/docs/quick-start#step-2") Quick start, step 2
      | ) and open it from there.
    li
      | Open
      strong Settings
      | . The line
      strong Web Push on this device
      | says
      code off
      | .
    li
      | Check the name in
      strong Name this device
      | (it is pre-filled, for example "Chrome on Windows") and press
      strong Enable notifications on this device
      | .
    li When the browser asks whether this site may send notifications, allow it. The line now says on.
    li
      | Press
      strong Send test notification
      | . The answer says how many devices it reached ("Sent to 2 device(s).") and a notification titled
      | "Buildyboy test notification" should appear.
  p
    | To stop notifications on a device, press
    strong Turn off for this device
    | on that device.
  h3#status What the status line means
  dl
    dt
      code on
      | /
      code off
    dd Notifications are, or are not, switched on for this browser.
    dt
      code blocked
    dd You (or the browser) refused permission earlier. Allow notifications for this site in the browser's site settings, then try again.
    dt
      code not supported here
    dd This browser cannot receive Web Push. On iPhone this means Buildyboy is not opened from the home screen.
  +callout(variant="warning")
    @content
      p
        strong iPhone and iPad:
        | Web Push only works in the app installed on the home screen, not in a Safari tab. If you would rather not install
        | it, use ntfy (below).
  p
    | Web Push also needs a secure address (https), which a deployed server has. On a plain
    code http://
    | address other than localhost, the page says the service worker is not active.

  h2#what-you-get What you are notified about
  p Under Send notifications for you can switch each kind off. All are on by default.
  dl
    dt
      strong Permission, question or plan waiting
    dd
      | A walk-mode request is waiting in the Inbox. Titles look like "Bash needs permission", "Claude is asking a
      | question" or "Plan waiting for approval". Permission notifications carry
      strong Allow
      | and
      strong Deny
      | buttons on platforms that support them; they work for 15 minutes.
    dt
      strong Turn finished (walk mode)
    dd "Turn finished — waiting for your next instruction".
    dt
      strong Job finished or failed
    dd
      | A job ended, for example "Job succeeded: Fix the flaky test". Jobs that you stopped yourself do not notify.
    dt
      strong Session went stale
    dd A working session has sent nothing for 10 minutes.
    dt
      strong Loop suspected
    dd The same failing call happened three or more times, or 15 turns went by with no file changes.
    dt
      strong CI result on a PR
    dd
      | The checks on a pull request passed or failed (needs a
      a(href="/docs/settings#github") GitHub token
      | ).
    dt
      strong Budget or rate limit
    dd A session or job is near its cost limit, or you are close to Claude's usage limits.
    dt
      strong Context nearly full
    dd A session's context is above your threshold (85% by default) or it has compacted three or more times.
  p
    | The text under each title is the project and the session name. Tapping a notification opens the Inbox (or the
    | relevant page) in an existing Buildyboy window if you have one. Press
    strong Save
    | after changing these switches.

  h2#quiet-hours Quiet hours
  p
    | Switch on
    strong Quiet hours
    | and choose
    strong From
    | and
    strong Until
    | (24-hour times, 22:00 to 07:00 by default) to silence notifications overnight. Requests still wait in the Inbox.
  +callout(variant="muted")
    @content
      p
        | Quiet hours follow the
        strong server's
        | clock. If the server is in a different time zone from you, adjust the times accordingly. The test notification
        | ignores quiet hours, so you can always test.

  h2#ntfy ntfy, the fallback
  p
    a(href="https://ntfy.sh") ntfy
    | is a free notification service with an app for Android and iPhone. Buildyboy can post to a topic there in addition
    | to Web Push. It is handy on an iPhone where Buildyboy is not installed, or as a second channel.
  ol
    li
      | Install the ntfy app and subscribe to a topic with a long, hard-to-guess name, for example
      code buildyboy-7f3k2q9x
      | . Anyone who knows the name can read it.
    li
      | In Buildyboy's Settings, paste the full address, for example
      code https://ntfy.sh/buildyboy-7f3k2q9x
      | , into
      strong ntfy topic URL
      | and press
      strong Save
      | .
    li
      strong Send test notification
      | now reports "and ntfy" too.
  p
    | ntfy messages are marked high priority for waiting requests. They have no Allow and Deny buttons; tap them to open
    | Buildyboy.

  h2#mute Muting one session
  p
    | A busy session can be muted without touching the rest: open it and switch off
    strong Notify
    | in its header. Every kind of notification about that session stops. It still appears in the Inbox and the
    | attention bar.

  h2#troubleshooting When notifications do not arrive
  ol
    li
      | Press
      strong Send test notification
      | . If it says "Sent to 0 device(s)", this device is not switched on: enable it again.
    li Check the phone's own settings: notifications allowed for the browser or the installed app, and no focus or do-not-disturb mode.
    li Check quiet hours and the per-kind switches in Settings, and the session's Notify switch.
    li
      | Remember walk-mode notifications only happen with walk mode on. With it off, nothing waits, so nothing is sent.
    li
      | Still nothing? See
      a(href="/docs/troubleshooting#no-notifications") Troubleshooting
      | .
